<title>VIETNAM: Laos to post modest increase in coffee output.</title>
<headline>Laos to post modest increase in coffee output.</headline>
<dateline>HO CHI MINH CITY, Vietnam 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Laos aims to double coffee production to 20,000 tonnes a year by 2000, double the current 10,000 tonnes, the head of the Association des Exportateurs Du Cafe in Laos said.</p>
<p>&quot;We hope to obtain in the year 2000 a yearly production of 20,000 tonnes,&quot; Bounlap Nhouyvanisvong said in a paper presented in French at the Asia Coffee conference here on Tuesday.</p>
<p>A translation of the paper was made available on Wednesday.</p>
<p>He put current Laotian coffee production at 10,000 tonnes. About 92 percent of output is robusta and eight percent arabica.</p>
<p>Up to 97 percent of total production is exported to Europe.</p>
</text>
